.DS_Store

# Ephemeral agent/sprint scratch artifacts (durable record lives in .diarie/tasks/)
#
# ANCHORED with a leading `/` — these are ROOT-level scratch files (`AGENT-03.md`, `RETRO-17.md`), and
# an unanchored pattern matches at ANY DEPTH. `AGENT-*.md` was silently swallowing the tracked, shipped
# `skills/swarm-wave/references/agent-concurrency-limits.md` (matching is case-insensitive — macOS sets
# `core.ignorecase=true`), which made it invisible to `check:md`: remark runs with
# `--ignore-path .gitignore` and `--frail`, so a file with warnings was never linted and the gate was
# green over it for as long as it existed. `check:tracked-ignored` now forbids that state outright.
#
# Do NOT anchor `PRIVATE-SYNERGY-*.md` below — for that one, matching at every depth IS the privacy
# invariant.
/AGENT-*.md
/RETRO-*.md
/SWARM-*.md
/SPIKE-*.md

# Local plugin/registry overrides
.claude/*.local.*
.claude/synergy-registry.local.json
.claude/vendor-registry.local.json

# Private SYNERGY overlays (proprietary↔public boundary). The PRIVATE- prefix
# keeps them OUTSIDE the public `SYNERGY-*.md` glob namespace, so no consumer
# can ever accidentally read them. Never commit: holds entries deliberately
# kept out of the public repo.
PRIVATE-SYNERGY-*.md

node_modules/

# Beads — fully local, ephemeral working state (not shared via git)
.beads/

# NOTE: the `.diarie/` tracker dir is dotted but COMMITTED, not ephemeral — it is
# the live task store (`diarie`), deliberately git-tracked and PR-reviewed. Unlike
# `.beads/` above it is NOT ignored; the dot marks committed project metadata (cf.
# `.claude/`, `.github/`), not throwaway state. Do not add it here.

# liggare's local register — a regenerable index (`liggare scan` rebuilds it), never content, so
# the whole dir stays out of git (the tracked ledger.sqlite + its WAL/SHM sidecars had otherwise
# shipped into every consumer plugin cache).
.liggare/
